module main;

// A kind-`*` binder is not applicable to a type argument. `[A]`
// has the default kind `*` (no leading stars), so writing `A(B)`
// in type position is a kind error: `A` has kind `*` and cannot
// consume an argument. Higher-kinded application `F(B)` is admitted
// only when the head's binder is annotated kind-`*→*` (`[*F]`).
// The diagnostic must point at `specs/grammar.md` § Kind grammar.
fn misapply[A][B](x: A(B)) -> A(B) { x }
